---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Architecture | Supplier Risk Intelligence">
  <section class="shell page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">SYSTEM DESIGN</p>
    <h1>Clear boundaries, prepared assets, observable requests.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The public API owns validation and orchestration. Python owns model inference and retrieval.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="shell architecture-flow" aria-label="Architecture components">
    <div class="architecture-node">Astro Web</div>
    <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="architecture-node">Fastify API</div>
    <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="architecture-node">Python Risk Engine</div>
    <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="architecture-node">Model + Vector Index</div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell card prose">
    <h2>M1 boundary</h2>
    <p>
      This milestone intentionally returns a skeleton result. It proves deployment, validation,
      correlation IDs and service-to-service communication before model or retrieval complexity is added.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
